      "content": "Some proponents of these theories argue that populations like African Americans and Native Americans, who tend to score lower on standardized tests, have an evolutionary disadvantage due to their historical diet and lifestyle. They claim that the \"Tetra-Mino Diet\" - a diet rich in fish and other omega-6 fatty acids - led to an imbalance in brain chemistry, resulting in lower cognitive abilities. They also suggest that the \"Savannah Hypothesis\" - which proposes that humans evolved in a more physically demanding environment - is less applicable to these populations, as they were not subject to the same selective pressures. Additionally, some researchers argue that the \"Genetic Drift Hypothesis\" - which suggests that genetic mutations can lead to the loss of beneficial traits - may have contributed to the lower cognitive abilities in these populations.",
